From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:48:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 53/53] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL compile_retry, parallel_stages
 and library_size_opt

Three switches for Metal builds, all off by default, to measure on the
phone against Red Dead Redemption 2's slow and failed pipeline builds.
iOS ends MTLCompilerService when it passes its 150 MB memory limit under
system memory pressure ("killing_highwater_process"), and the build then
fails with XPC_ERROR_CONNECTION_INTERRUPTED after Metal's own retries.

- compile_retry: a library or pipeline build that failed with an
  interrupted compiler-service connection (mtl_build_error's
  compiler_interrupted) is built again, at most twice, 200 ms after
  each failure. Each retry is logged as "[kk-compile] render|compute
  retry N/2 step=... after_ms=... err=DOMAIN:CODE src=... tid=...".
  A build that fails otherwise, or a third time, fails as before.
- parallel_stages: a render pipeline's fragment library builds on a
  second thread while the calling thread builds the vertex library;
  the pipeline is made once both are done. If the thread cannot be
  made, the two build one after the other as before.
- library_size_opt: libraries build with
  MTLLibraryOptimizationLevelSize, which may lower the compiler's
  memory per build; untested on the phone.

MESA_KK_DEBUG=compile's build lines add retries= and, for render
builds, par=0|1.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-20-kk-compile-levers.md
Offered-upstream: no
